#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# full_form

#% text
# `full_form(x)` shows `x` with every part written as a plain call: `x + y^2` as `add(x, pow(y, 2))`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `full_form` stays around the value as a wrapper that changes only how it is shown.

#% item
# It shows the structure functions such as `part`, `head` and `level` work on.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
full_form(x + y^2)
#% output
#= add(x, pow(y, 2))

#% cell
full_form([1, a*b])
#% output
#= list(1, mul(a, b))

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Divisions and the exponential:

#% cell
full_form(a/b)
#% output
#= mul(a, pow(b, -1))

#% cell
full_form(exp(x))
#% output
#= pow(e, x)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `head` gives the outermost call shown:

#% cell
head(x + y^2)
#% output
#= add

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `input_form`, `head`, `level`, `to_string`
